                <pb facs="0871" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.75 National Telephone Co./323: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-15T19:00:00-05:00">March 15, 1940—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Your 48, March 14, 4 p.m. We are at a loss to understand this change in
                    attitude on the part of the Spanish Government. We feel that it is high time
                    that the Spanish Government acquiesce in a fair and reasonable settlement of
                    this matter and we are confident that you will continue your efforts to that
                    end.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
